<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_trinket_16.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Protection Paladin Trinkets in Phase 3</span></h2>Your trinket usage will be dictated by the demands of your encounter and the capabilities of you and your group. However, none of the tank trinkets available this tier make a strong case for being worn by themselves, meaning we will usually end up running an offensive trinket loadout which is only swapped in the most dire of circumstances.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets:</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96873/primordius-talisman-of-rage">
<img alt="Primordius' Talisman of Rage" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Primordius' Talisman of Rage</span></a> (Proc) — A very reliable strength boost with decent passive crit, which can be reforged to haste. While the item doesn't really seem great at first glance, it ends up being our most reliable option for damage overall this tier.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96543/gaze-of-the-twins">
<img alt="Gaze of the Twins" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_spectralsight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaze of the Twins</span></a> (Proc) — Same to the previous item, but different. How strong the item performs depends a lot on how offensive your loadup is overall, but generally speaking, it should outperform the competition.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=94508/brutal-talisman-of-the-shado-pan-assault">
<img alt="Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_strengthofarms.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Brutal Talisman of the Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> (Proc) — Despite not making it into any of the BiS lists, this trinket is a sleeper hit. Performing very close to the BiS options, it can acquired reliably from the <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1435/shado-pan-assault">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Shado-Pan Assault</span></a> and the high expertise and strength proc are both great while you're still acquiring gear.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96770/spark-of-zandalar">
<img alt="Spark of Zandalar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_lightningshield.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Spark of Zandalar</span></a> (Proc) — High passive Haste is interesting, but the long ramp and unreliable effect will make it miss out on its full potential more often than not.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96842/fabled-feather-of-ji-kun">
<img alt="Fabled Feather of Ji-Kun" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_priest_angelicfeather.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fabled Feather of Ji-Kun</span></a> (Proc) — A very strong strength proc makes this item stand out from the competition, but due to stat inflation we are unable to make any use of the high passive hit.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets:</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96927/soul-barrier">
<img alt="Soul Barrier" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Barrier</span></a> (Active) — High Stamina is always great, the on-use effect sadly is often not. Despite this, it still is the most relevant defensive trinket of this phase.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96421/fortitude-of-the-zandalari">
<img alt="Fortitude of the Zandalari" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_mindvision.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fortitude of the Zandalari</span></a> (Active) — Similar to other battlemaster trinkets, the item is good when used with a concrete use-case and goal in mind, but not well-statted enough to wear all the time.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=91210/tyrannical-gladiators-emblem-of-tenacity">
<img alt="Tyrannical Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_endlessrage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Tyrannical Gladiator's Emblem of Tenacity</span></a> (Active) — In this case, a rose by another name <i>does</i> smell as sweet. Both battlemaster trinkets are very similar in power and can be used interchangeably, but not together, as they share their cooldown between each other, but not with other trinkets.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="reputation">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reputation for Protection Paladins in Phase 3</span></h2>In Phase 3, most faction rewards are only relevant to acquire some early catch-up gear, but the majority of the rewards are replaced even by Celestial Dungeon rewards. A notable exception is the raid faction <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/faction=1435/shado-pan-assault">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Shado-Pan Assault</span></a>, which provides normal raid quality items. Notably, the reputation can be farmed before progressing the raid proper by farming raid trash, completing quests on the Isle of Thunder and acquiring <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95496/shado-pan-assault-insignia">
