<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Protection Paladin</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit (or 2550 Hit Rating), whereas for Expertise the caps are split into 7.5% Expertise (or 2550 Expertise Rating) to reach the so-called "soft cap", and 15% Expertise (or 5100 Expertise Rating) to reach the true "hard cap". Keep in mind that some abilities such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your melee hits can no longer miss Raid bosses. Spells, however, operate on a different Hit table and it would require additional investment into Hit to negate this miss chance entirely. In Mists of Pandaria, there exists another option: most tanks will now look to solve their Spell Hit woes through Expertise.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>At 7.5% Expertise, Raid bosses will no longer be able to Dodge your attack, but they can still Parry them. For most Raid encounters, reaching the soft cap is sufficient. However,  you may aim to reach the full 15% Expertise cap to eliminate both Dodge and Parry from the equation. Since the value of expertise is relatively close to other stats, this is not a big loss and increases your consistency across fights. There are exceptions, though: Some Raid bosses either cannot Parry due to encounter mechanics or positioning, and can therefore be dealt with in such a way that parries aren't a concern. In those cases, it may be wise to reforge or swap gear to favor other stats.<br/>
<br/>Additionally, reaching 7.5% Expertise will also make you achieve Spell Hit cap, ensuring your spells such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=26573/consecration">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_innerfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Consecration</span></a> won't miss.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c2" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Protection Paladin</span></h2>Reaching the Expertise soft cap remains a top priority, and while you initially often had to rely on <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76693/precise-primordial-ruby">
<img alt="Precise Primordial Ruby" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_red.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Precise Primordial Ruby</span></a> to get there, this becomes much less of an effort once you start acquiring gear in raids. Because of this, we can afford to shift more of our gems towards <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76699/quick-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Quick Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Quick Sun's Radiance</span></a>. However, it's usually worth aiming for socket bonuses that grant Expertise, Hit, Haste, or Stamina in roughly that order of priority. To meet those bonuses efficiently, make use of hybrid gems like <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76667/wicked-vermilion-onyx">
<img alt="Wicked Vermilion Onyx" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_orange.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Wicked Vermilion Onyx</span></a>, <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76681/accurate-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Accurate Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Accurate Imperial Amethyst</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76642/lightning-wild-jade">
<img alt="Lightning Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Lightning Wild Jade</span></a>. On certain encounters with high spike damage you may want to consider swapping in more <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76639/solid-rivers-heart">
<img alt="Solid River's Heart" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_blue.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Solid River's Heart</span></a>  or <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76700/fractured-suns-radiance">
<img alt="Fractured Sun's Radiance" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_yellow.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fractured Sun's Radiance</span></a> to bolster your defenses. <br/>
<br/>Additionally, with Phase 3 of Mists of Pandaria you will gain access to legendary meta gems by progressing your legendary quest line. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> is the default choice due to its generous uptime, relegating <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> to an option only considered in extremely greedy, damage-focused setups where you've basically already exhausted all other options.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
